{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfhXq9BMLbJi9LTVKexv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Result:** Dq ≈ 433 cm⁻¹ (Δt ≈ 4 330 cm⁻¹) and B ≈ 878 cm⁻¹. These values reproduce all three observed bands to within about 3 cm⁻¹. I did this calculation by hand and did not use the fitting tools.\n\n**Setting up the model**\n\nA tetrahedral d⁷ ion uses the same quartet energy matrix as an octahedral d³ ion. The two are related by the hole formalism together with the sign change of Δ between octahedral and tetrahedral fields. The ground term is therefore ⁴A₂(F), and the three spin-allowed bands are assigned as follows:\n\n- ν₁ = ⁴A₂ → ⁴T₂(F). Its energy is 10Dq.\n- ν₂ = ⁴A₂ → ⁴T₁(F).\n- ν₃ = ⁴A₂ → ⁴T₁(P).\n\nThe two ⁴T₁ states mix. Their energies are:\n\nE(⁴T₁) = 7.5B + 15Dq ∓ ½·√(225B² + 100Dq² − 180B·Dq)\n\nAdding the two roots cancels the square root, so ν₂ + ν₃ = 15B + 30Dq.\n\n**Solving**\n\n1. From the first band, 10Dq = 4 330 cm⁻¹, so Dq = 433 cm⁻¹.\n2. Adding the second and third bands gives ν₂ + ν₃ = 7 520 + 18 640 = 26 160 cm⁻¹.\n3. Substituting: 15B = 26 160 − 12 990 = 13 170 cm⁻¹, so B ≈ 878 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Checking the fit**\n\nWith Dq = 433 cm⁻¹ and B = 878 cm⁻¹:\n\n- The centre term is 7.5B + 15Dq = 6 585 + 6 495 = 13 080 cm⁻¹.\n- The square root is √(1.2377 × 10⁸) ≈ 11 125 cm⁻¹, so half of it is about 5 563 cm⁻¹.\n- This gives ν₂ ≈ 7 518 cm⁻¹ (observed 7 520) and ν₃ ≈ 18 643 cm⁻¹ (observed 18 640).\n\n**Interpretation**\n\nThe free Co²⁺ ion has B ≈ 1 115 cm⁻¹, so the nephelauxetic ratio is β ≈ 878 / 1 115 ≈ 0.79. This indicates moderate covalency in the metal–ligand bonds, which is typical for tetrahedral Co(II).\n\nThe Racah parameter C cannot be determined from these data. All three bands lie within the quartet manifold, and those energies depend only on Dq and B.\n\n{\"Dq\": 433, \"B\": 878, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Quartet bands fixed Dq = ν1/10 and B from ν2+ν3 = 15B+30Dq; C is not determinable from spin-allowed bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7974,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7974,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11527cdc-c148-4f3b-a929-6e5c50e16365","uuid":"7b69018b-0cd5-4e77-8dbf-e583493ecf7c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T08:44:13.317Z","request_id":"req_011CgfhXpk7QhN1NUL7zHsZC"}
